  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of State has obligated $126M on contracts so far in FY2027 to date. The Department of State processed 1,725 awards, with an average award size of $73.3K. Obligations fell 98.7% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior totals much larger: FY22 totaled $12B, FY23 totaled $11.7B, FY24 totaled $11.7B, FY25 totaled $9.8B, and FY26 totaled $9.8B. The FY2027 to date picture is therefore a sharp reduction in obligations compared with recent full fiscal years. Current-year totals are partial, because the period reported is fiscal year to date. The available NAICS breakdown for FY2027 to date highlights Security Guards and Patrol Services with $25.7M and Facilities Support Services with $18.4M. The vendor list for FY2027 to date shows MISCELLANEOUS FOREIGN AWARDEES at $8.4M and PUTZ SECURITY AG at $6.2M among the top recipients. This snapshot highlights where limited FY2027 contracting dollars have concentrated so far.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does current spending compare to recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "The Department of State obligated $126M in FY2027 to date, compared with $12B in FY22. The Department of State obligated $11.7B in FY23 and $11.7B in FY24. The Department of State obligated $9.8B in FY25 and $9.8B in FY26, so obligations fell 98.7% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What categories and vendors are receiving FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services received $25.7M and Facilities Support Services received $18.4M in FY2027 to date. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services received $7.2M and Other Computer Related Services received $7.1M. MISCELLANEOUS FOREIGN AWARDEES received $8.4M and PUTZ SECURITY AG received $6.2M among top vendors."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of State spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of State has obligated $126M on contracts so far in FY2027 to date. The Department of State obligated 1,725 awards with an average award size of $73.3K. Current-year totals are partial because the period reported is fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does State buy?",
      "a": "The Department of State is buying security, facilities, consulting, and travel-related services in FY2027 to date. Security Guards and Patrol Services received $25.7M, Facilities Support Services received $18.4M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services received $7.2M, and Other Computer Related Services received $7.1M, among other categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are State's largest contractors?",
      "a": "MISCELLANEOUS FOREIGN AWARDEES and PUTZ SECURITY AG are the largest vendors so far in FY2027 to date. MISCELLANEOUS FOREIGN AWARDEES received $8.4M and PUTZ SECURITY AG received $6.2M, followed by ARK GROUP DMCC at $5.8M and KBR SERVICES, LLC at $5.2M."
